{"name":"Less Traveled","hex":"#5d6957","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"less","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["comparative degree of little","Used for constructing syntactic diminutive comparatives of adjectives and adverbs."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["comparative form of little: more little; of inferior size, degree or extent; smaller, lesser. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A smaller amount of; not as much."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/less"},{"term":"traveled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Frequented by travelers.","Experienced in travel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of travel"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traveled"}],"entries":[{"title":"Travel","blocks":[{"text":"Travel is the movement of people between distant geographical locations. Travel can be done by foot, bicycle, automobile, train, boat, bus, airplane, ship or other means; with or without luggage; and can be one way or round trip. Travel can also include relatively short stays between successive movements, as in the case of tourism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Cross_Harbour_Tunnel_%281%29.JPG/330px-Cross_Harbour_Tunnel_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travel","wikidata":"Q61509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Rush_hour%2C_Hong_Kong_MTR.jpg/500px-Rush_hour%2C_Hong_Kong_MTR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Rush_hour%2C_Hong_Kong_MTR.jpg/500px-Rush_hour%2C_Hong_Kong_MTR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARush_hour%2C_Hong_Kong_MTR.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi